adjudication.rationale:
The diff adds `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts` with an auth check:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset (i.e., `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET === undefined`) and the request also omits the header (so the header lookup returns `undefined`), the comparison becomes `undefined !== undefined`, which is `false`, so the request is accepted and proceeds to credential create/update. This is a real auth-bypass condition when `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` is true but the secret is not configured.
